<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       UNBLOCK RESEARCH THAT MRR AUTO-GENERATION MAKES IMPOSSIBLE

       More Realistic Research auto-generates analysis requirements for any
       project it does not list, and it picks the study subjects from the
       things that project UNLOCKS. For Industrial and Spacer tiers those
       subjects must be REVERSE-ENGINEERED, meaning you have to possess one.

       Which you cannot, because the research is what lets you build it.

       Usually this is survivable, because UnlockedDefs also contains recipe
       products you can find, buy or loot, and analysis points pool per TYPE
       so any one obtainable subject satisfies the whole requirement. It only
       bites when EVERY unlocked thing is player-built-only.

       MRR's author clearly knew: their 46 hand-authored entries are almost
       exactly the vanilla projects that would otherwise dead-end
       (WatermillGenerator, Xenogermination, GeothermalPower, MoisturePump,
       GunTurrets, Biosculpting, GrowthVats, SterileMaterials...). This file
       covers what their hand-curated list missed, which is one vanilla
       project plus whatever our modded load order adds.

       `python tools/audit_research.py` regenerates the candidate list.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <!-- MULTIANALYZER. The one that matters.

       Its only study subjects are the multi-analyzer itself plus three
       modded variants (GravDecreasePylon_GT, GravIncreasePylon_GT,
       VGE_CompactMultiAnalyzer). Verified by hand: none appears in any
       structure layout, prefab, scatterer or loot table; the ThingDef has no
       tradeTags and no trader stocks the BuildingsMisc category; and the one
       reward-table reference to "MultiAnalyzer" is a
       ThingSetMaker_Conditional_ResearchFinished gating AIPersonaCore on
       having already done the research. So there is no way to obtain one.

       This is load-bearing for the whole run: USE_GE_ProjectBase lists
       MultiAnalyzer as a requiredResearchFacility, so an unresearchable
       multi-analyzer means the entire Ushanka glittertech tree is
       unreachable no matter what Archinity.Glitterites does.

       Experimental on the components it is actually built from, which is
       what auto-generation would have used for its Experimental pool anyway.
       Industrial components, not spacer: this is an Industrial project and
       should not need spacer-tier goods to unlock. -->
  <ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef>
    <defName>Archinity_Unblock_MultiAnalyzer</defName>
    <researchProject>MultiAnalyzer</researchProject>
    <experimentalMaterials>
      <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
    </experimentalMaterials>
    <experimentalPointsRequired>3</experimentalPointsRequired>
  </ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef>

</Defs>
